<title>THAILAND: Bank of Thailand says reference rate 29.945.</title>
<headline>Bank of Thailand says reference rate 29.945.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Thailand on Monday announced that the weighted average interbank exchange rate was 29.945 per dollar against 29.155 on Friday.</p>
<p>The reference rate is the average rate traded the previous day. It has been announced daily by the central bank since last week's managed flotation of the baht.</p>
<p>The baht was quoted at 30.55/30.85 to the dollar onshore and 30.10/30.30 in offshore markets early.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
